SPRINT SUCCESS CRITERIA (Definition of Done)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

ALL of the following MUST be true for sprint completion:

✅ 1. TWS category fully removed
   - No "true-wireless-tws" in slugToIdMap
   - No TWS catalogueItem in Sanity
   - TWS products archived (not deleted)
   - TWS semantic rules removed

✅ 2. Four new categories added and functional
   - semi-open resolves to ID
   - bluetooth-dac-amps resolves to ID
   - usb-c-dacs resolves to ID
   - eartips resolves to ID
   - All have semantic rules
   - All appear in navigation

✅ 3. Category renames applied
   - "In-Ear & Wireless" → "In-Ear Monitors"
   - "Monitors (IEMs)" → "Universal IEMs"
   - "Maintenance" → "Fit & Comfort"

✅ 4. VFS index valid
   - Build succeeds without errors
   - 23 leaf categories in slugToIdMap
   - All subtree queries work correctly
   - No orphaned children references

✅ 5. Regression tests pass
   - tests/regression/catalogue-coherence-sprint.regression.test.ts: ALL PASS
   - tests/integration/catalogue-to-products.test.ts: ALL PASS
   - tests/unit/vfs/descendant-unrolling.test.ts: ALL PASS

✅ 6. Application runs correctly
   - npm run dev starts without errors
   - Navigation shows correct structure
   - No console errors related to categories

✅ 7. Documentation updated
   - Sprint summary created
   - Category structure documented
   - Audit report generated

