═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
EMERGENCY ROLLBACK PROCEDURE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

If critical failure occurs:

1. STOP: Do not continue making changes
2. RESTORE: Revert data/catalogue-index.json from git
   git checkout data/catalogue-index.json
3. RESTORE: Revert semanticConfig.ts from git
   git checkout lib/catalogue/semanticConfig.ts
4. VERIFY: Run regression tests to confirm baseline restored
5. DOCUMENT: Record what failed in sprint summary

For Sanity CMS changes (harder to revert):
- Keep detailed notes of all document IDs created/modified
- Manual restoration through Studio may be required
- Consider using Sanity CLI for scripted backup/restore

